<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Nájera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1367</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Navarrete · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castilian-civil-war">Castilian Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najera">Nájera</a> was fought on 3 April 1367 in La Rioja during the Castilian civil war. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-black-prince">Edward the Black Prince</a>, with an Anglo-Gascon army, restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-castile">Peter I of Castile</a> by defeating his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-castile">Henry of Trastámara</a> and the French captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrand-du-guesclin">Bertrand du Guesclin</a>, who was captured. Henry returned two years later and killed Peter after Montiel.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-najera.jpg" alt="Battle of Nájera" width="320" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Loyset Liédet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_najera_froissart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
